factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The article gives the bear incident date as 21 (no month), but the draft's reel_script and caption state it as October 21 (அக்டோபர் 21 / அக். 21), an invented month.
  The reel_script says the bear incident happened 'in this same village' (இதே கிராமத்தில்), which matches the article (Tharkadu village), so this is fine; however the slide's claim that the bear 'entered the town' (ஊருக்குள் புகுந்தது) is not an exact match to the article's phrasing that it entered a woman's path and chased her into forest, so the bear's behavior is loosely paraphrased.
  The caption and reel_script say the bear chased the woman who had bought milk, but the article says the bear entered the village and chased the woman who had bought milk and then went into the forest; the reel_script omits that the bear went into the forest area, which is minor.
  The reel_script says the elephant entered 'lands within the Chembalai Sivilikaradu lake irrigation area' (செம்மலை சிவிலிகரடு ஏரி பாசனப் பகுதி), which matches the article, but the reel_script omits that the elephant broke stone pillars and wire fences in Mani's and Raghunathan's land as an action in the same sentence, so the damage to fences is mixed with the lake/irrigation clause, creating two facts in one sentence.
